(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #109. `_list_append`'s new refusal compares the list
 POINTER against `_released_list_header`'s own address, not the list's
 shape - a real list genuinely reaching `length == capacity` mid-growth
 looks exactly like the released header at that instant (both have
 length == capacity), and only an identity check tells them apart. A list
 literal's capacity is always >= 8 (max(elements.len(), 8)), so this pushes
 a real list through its first growth/realloc to prove the refusal did not
 also catch real, legitimate growth.)

a list called nums is [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8].
print nums's length.
append 9 to nums.
append 10 to nums.
On error print "should not refuse a real list".
print nums's length.
